  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1223 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nAfter a cool day Friday, clouds are expected to clear by Friday\nnight, allowing for lows in the mid 20s to mid 30s. Similar\nconditions are expected each night through Sunday night. \nFrost/freeze conditions are expected across much or all of the \narea, with the worst of it being over the typical cold spots in \nthe eastern CWA. There are models (especially the REFS and RRFS)\nshowing high clouds moving in Friday night and keeping temps a\nfew degrees warmer, so that will have to be monitored. Frost/freeze\nheadlines will be addressed in future shifts if the forecast \nstays on track.\n\nThe rest of the long term is dry.\n\nTemperatures will trend warmer through the long term, starting\nwith highs in the 50s. Highs will be closer to normal in the 60s\non Sunday, then upper 60s to around 70 through the rest of the \nlong term forecast period.",
